& [DictatedIntent]
  + the only seed needed to initiate a complete Cantor-managed runtime installation should be the Cantor bootstrap runtime plus Cantor SOP
  + the seed should explode or inflate into every file that is installed and used by the selected Cantor runtime
  + backup therefore preserves the compact initiating runtime and semantic declaration rather than accumulated development-build caches

& [RuntimeClosure]
  + runtime closure means the complete transitive set of Cantor-managed files identities configurations trust material public metadata provider adapters model artifacts and generated state required to start and operate one selected runtime profile
  + every member of the runtime closure must be declared derived built acquired verified or explicitly supplied under the installation SOP
  + every materialized member must have a content identity provenance authority role target location compatibility boundary and installation receipt
  + no undeclared local file ambient path mutable download or previously cached artifact may silently enter the runtime closure

& [TwoPartSeed]
  + seed part one is a small admitted Cantor bootstrap runtime able to parse verify plan materialize and receipt the installation SOP
  + seed part two is a Cantor SOP installation contract that declares the selected runtime closure and every derivation acquisition verification layout activation and recovery rule
  + the bootstrap runtime and SOP seed must remain independently identifiable and jointly sufficient to begin inflation when their declared material sources and host prerequisites are available

& [Materialization]
  + source-buildable artifacts may be compiled from exact admitted source toolchain dependency and build identities
  + externally authored binaries libraries model weights and other irreducible bytes must be acquired from declared content-addressed sources or an admitted offline artifact pack and verified before use
  + generated configuration trust stores semantic packages service topology and runtime indexes must be deterministically derived where possible and independently verified
  + installation completes only after exact layout permission compatibility trust and runtime acceptance gates pass and one complete receipt closes the realized graph

& [CustodyAndPrerequisites]
  + private keys credentials and other secrets remain external custody inputs referenced but never embedded or regenerated by SOP
  + operating system drivers hardware firmware and artifact transport are explicit host prerequisites unless a later broader machine-installation contract imports them
  + network availability is not assumed; an air-gapped profile may admit a content-addressed artifact pack beside the two-part seed
  + missing unavailable untrusted incompatible or unauthorized material must refuse without substituting a remote fallback or weakening the selected profile

& [DevelopmentCacheBoundary]
  + Cargo targets incremental objects debug symbols repeated proof-campaign builds logs and other replaceable development caches are not members of the runtime closure unless a later warm-development profile imports an exact bounded subset
  + the current D:\CantorBuilds accumulation is development sediment and must not be treated as unique semantic state or a required backup payload
  + historical proof may retain source commit commands artifact hashes and receipts without retaining every replaceable build byte

& [AcceptanceDirection]
  + from a clean admitted host with the bootstrap runtime the installation SOP and every declared reachable material source the installer must reproduce the selected runtime closure without hidden local dependencies
  + a complete audit must enumerate every runtime file and trace it backward to the seed through derivation acquisition or explicit-supply edges
  + deletion of replaceable build caches must not prevent reinflation after required toolchain dependency and artifact sources are restored

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical specification satisfaction signature Rust implementation artifact download model acquisition secret access installation activation cleanup cache deletion remote machine operation FPGA work Minecraft work or physical effect is authorized
